            <ArticleTitle>Accessory spleen torsion: US, CT and MR findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>509-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Torsion of an accessory spleen is a very unusual entity that can appear with abdominal pain associated with the presence of an avascular mass. We report the case of a 13-year-old boy with torsion and infarction of an accessory spleen presenting as a painful abdominal mass in which imaging examination with US, CT and MR showed a large avascular mass in the upper left abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
